// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`EV-1 rulebook v3 > renders every number, deterministically 1`] = `
"## Training rulebook (rulebook.v3)

| Goal | Sets | Reps |
|-|-|-|
| Build muscle | 3–4 | 8–12 |
| Lose weight | 2–3 | 12–15 |
| Stay fit | 2–3 | 10–15 |

| Experience | Exercise levels | Starting hold |
|-|-|-|
| Newbie | beginner | 20 s |
| Moderately regular | beginner, intermediate | 30 s |
| Experienced | beginner, intermediate, expert | 45 s |

- Newbies use the minimum of the sets range; when that cannot fill the session, the request says so and the full range applies.
- Order: warmup → compound → isolation → cardio → cooldown.
- Warm-up 300 s and cool-down 300 s are always included and count toward the session.
- The plan fills 85–100% of the session length. When the candidates cannot fill that, the request's time window is lowered; then use nearly every candidate at the top of its range.
- When the focus overlaps a recent workout, keep about half of its exercises for continuity.
- After a Reset, at least half of the main exercises differ from the reset plan.
- Cardio: when Cardio is a chosen focus, or when you choose the focus (any goal), placed before the cool-down.
- When you choose the focus: Lose weight may add a cardio block; Build muscle and Stay fit at most 1 cardio exercise, continuous cardio 300–600 s.
- Continuous cardio: 1 set of 300–1800 s, within the request's continuous_cardio_s range; no more cardio exercises than max_cardio_items (null = no limit).
- Progression: cap 15 reps / 60 s; step +2 reps / +10 s; minimum 6 reps / 15 s.
- After a Reset, follow the reason:
  - too_long: Aim near the 85% lower bound of the time window with fewer exercises.
  - too_hard: Use lighter volume or easier versions.
  - too_easy: Use more volume or harder versions.
  - dislike_exercises: Use different exercises."
`;
